1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,225
Look at this path at eight in the morning.

2
00:00:03,245 --> 00:00:05,388
Two coffee carts are already open.

3
00:00:05,408 --> 00:00:08,633
Customers walk past both prices and buy
from the

4
00:00:08,653 --> 00:00:09,513
cheaper one.

5
00:00:09,533 --> 00:00:13,839
So if A cuts its price, B loses customers
even if B

6
00:00:13,859 --> 00:00:14,720
does nothing.

7
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:16,178
Here is the idea.

8
00:00:16,198 --> 00:00:19,095
When what you take home depends on someone

9
00:00:19,115 --> 00:00:21,647
else's choice, we call that a game.

10
00:00:21,667 --> 00:00:24,928
That is all the word means in this unit.

11
00:00:24,948 --> 00:00:29,668
It is not a board game, and it is not
about who is

12
00:00:29,688 --> 00:00:30,543
clever.

13
00:00:30,563 --> 00:00:33,460
These two carts just cannot ignore each
other.

14
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:35,558
Here is what we will do.

15
00:00:35,578 --> 00:00:39,403
First we check that the two carts are
already in a

16
00:00:39,423 --> 00:00:40,246
game.

17
00:00:40,266 --> 00:00:41,994
Then we name the players.

18
00:00:42,014 --> 00:00:44,791
Then we name the strategies, High or Low.

19
00:00:44,811 --> 00:00:48,287
Last we name the payoffs, what each pair
of prices

20
00:00:48,307 --> 00:00:49,130
pays.

21
00:00:49,150 --> 00:00:53,125
That is all I need you to see in this
opening.

22
00:00:53,145 --> 00:00:57,119
Don't pick a price for them yet, and don't
guess who

23
00:00:57,139 --> 00:00:58,209
would cut first.

24
00:00:58,229 --> 00:01:00,025
We only describe the morning.

25
00:01:00,045 --> 00:01:02,930
Next we start with those two carts again.

26
00:01:03,150 --> 00:01:05,492
Look at those two carts again.

27
00:01:05,512 --> 00:01:10,215
Cart A is thinking, I will cut the price
and sell more.

28
00:01:10,235 --> 00:01:14,151
Fine, if A is the only cart on the path.

29
00:01:14,171 --> 00:01:15,725
B is already there.

30
00:01:15,745 --> 00:01:18,087
Customers walk to the cheaper board.

31
00:01:18,107 --> 00:01:22,810
So when A sells more, those cups used to
stop at B.

32
00:01:22,830 --> 00:01:24,302
Here is the idea.

33
00:01:24,322 --> 00:01:27,658
What one cart takes home that hour depends
on

34
00:01:27,677 --> 00:01:29,895
both prices, not just its own.

35
00:01:29,915 --> 00:01:31,013
Try a test.

36
00:01:31,033 --> 00:01:33,251
Pretend the other cart is gone.

37
00:01:33,271 --> 00:01:37,353
If what you take home does not change, you
are not

38
00:01:37,372 --> 00:01:38,844
in a game yet.

39
00:01:38,864 --> 00:01:42,200
You just have a shop on an empty path.

40
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:44,018
Think of one cart first.

41
00:01:44,038 --> 00:01:47,291
Customers have nowhere else to buy, so
that cart

42
00:01:47,311 --> 00:01:49,837
can set a price and ignore everyone.

43
00:01:49,857 --> 00:01:52,382
On this path there are two carts.

44
00:01:52,402 --> 00:01:55,655
Customers look at both prices and walk to
the

45
00:01:55,675 --> 00:01:56,547
cheaper one.

46
00:01:56,567 --> 00:01:59,820
Each cart has to think about the other
board.

47
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:00,885
Now watch B.

48
00:02:00,905 --> 00:02:03,726
A puts a lower price on the board.

49
00:02:03,746 --> 00:02:06,212
B leaves its price where it is.

50
00:02:06,232 --> 00:02:07,988
Customers walk over to A.

51
00:02:08,008 --> 00:02:11,894
B did not touch the board, and B still
takes home

52
00:02:11,914 --> 00:02:12,959
less that hour.

53
00:02:12,979 --> 00:02:15,800
That is all I need you to see.

54
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:16,950
Use two checks.

55
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:20,398
Can I say what this cart takes home
without

56
00:02:20,418 --> 00:02:21,931
mentioning the other one?

57
00:02:21,951 --> 00:02:25,763
If the other board changes and this board
does not,

58
00:02:25,783 --> 00:02:28,445
does this cart still take home less?

59
00:02:28,465 --> 00:02:32,277
If both answers are no, you can ignore the
other

60
00:02:32,297 --> 00:02:33,154
cart.

61
00:02:33,174 --> 00:02:35,070
Next we name the players.

62
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:39,017
We already know the two carts cannot
ignore each

63
00:02:39,037 --> 00:02:39,894
other.

64
00:02:39,914 --> 00:02:42,385
That makes this morning a game.

65
00:02:42,405 --> 00:02:44,046
Now name the players.

66
00:02:44,066 --> 00:02:48,198
A player is someone who posts a price this
morning.

67
00:02:48,218 --> 00:02:50,689
The market is not a player.

68
00:02:50,709 --> 00:02:53,180
The weather is not a player.

69
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,610
Here is the idea.

70
00:02:54,630 --> 00:02:58,184
A player is someone who posts a price, and
who

71
00:02:58,204 --> 00:03:00,329
cares what the other cart posts.

72
00:03:00,349 --> 00:03:04,261
If it cannot post a price, it is not a
player.

73
00:03:04,281 --> 00:03:06,763
Rain can change how many customers come.

74
00:03:06,783 --> 00:03:09,980
Rain does not put a number on a board.

75
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,115
Look at the three names.

76
00:03:12,135 --> 00:03:14,249
Cart A posts a price.

77
00:03:14,269 --> 00:03:16,384
Cart B posts a price.

78
00:03:16,404 --> 00:03:20,226
Customers look at both boards and walk to
the

79
00:03:20,246 --> 00:03:21,124
cheaper cart.

80
00:03:21,144 --> 00:03:23,258
The customers are the crowd.

81
00:03:23,278 --> 00:03:25,820
They are not a third player.

82
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:28,990
Someone writes, the market chooses the
winner.

83
00:03:29,010 --> 00:03:30,349
Cross that out.

84
00:03:30,369 --> 00:03:32,614
A and B post prices.

85
00:03:32,634 --> 00:03:33,519
Customers walk.

86
00:03:33,539 --> 00:03:38,954
There is no third board on this path, so
there is no

87
00:03:38,974 --> 00:03:39,860
third player.

88
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:44,665
Before you keep a name, ask whether it can
post a

89
00:03:44,685 --> 00:03:45,976
price this morning.

90
00:03:45,996 --> 00:03:48,160
If it cannot, drop it.

91
00:03:48,180 --> 00:03:49,471
Two names stay.

92
00:03:49,491 --> 00:03:51,655
Cart A and Cart B.

93
00:03:51,675 --> 00:03:53,839
Next we name the strategies.

94
00:03:53,859 --> 00:03:55,150
High or Low.

95
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:57,167
We know the players.

96
00:03:57,187 --> 00:03:59,502
Cart A and Cart B.

97
00:03:59,522 --> 00:04:01,369
Now name the strategies.

98
00:04:01,389 --> 00:04:05,104
Be aggressive does not tell a customer
which

99
00:04:05,124 --> 00:04:06,971
number is written there.

100
00:04:06,991 --> 00:04:07,905
High does.

101
00:04:07,925 --> 00:04:08,838
Low does.

102
00:04:08,858 --> 00:04:13,040
A strategy has to be something you can
actually

103
00:04:13,060 --> 00:04:13,920
post.

104
00:04:13,940 --> 00:04:15,459
Here is the idea.

105
00:04:15,479 --> 00:04:19,306
A strategy is what this morning already
allows you to

106
00:04:19,326 --> 00:04:20,184
post.

107
00:04:20,204 --> 00:04:22,492
No peeking at the other board.

108
00:04:22,512 --> 00:04:25,186
No third price at the last second.

109
00:04:25,206 --> 00:04:28,648
No speech to the queue instead of a
number.

110
00:04:28,668 --> 00:04:33,650
If it is not on the list, it is not a
strategy here.

111
00:04:33,670 --> 00:04:36,499
Write the list before the customers
arrive.

112
00:04:36,519 --> 00:04:40,162
Keep only what this morning allows, and
cross out

113
00:04:40,182 --> 00:04:41,057
the slogans.

114
00:04:41,077 --> 00:04:44,720
For each cart that list is High or Low.

115
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:47,162
Nothing else is on the board.

116
00:04:47,182 --> 00:04:48,790
That gives four pairs.

117
00:04:48,810 --> 00:04:53,167
Before you keep a phrase, ask whether it
is High or

118
00:04:53,187 --> 00:04:54,038
Low.

119
00:04:54,058 --> 00:04:57,221
If it is not, you changed the game.

120
00:04:57,241 --> 00:04:59,609
Keep the list short on purpose.

121
00:04:59,629 --> 00:05:03,190
Next we name the payoffs on those four
pairs.

122
00:05:03,340 --> 00:05:06,786
We know the players, and we know the
strategies

123
00:05:06,806 --> 00:05:08,326
are High or Low.

124
00:05:08,346 --> 00:05:09,867
Now name the payoffs.

125
00:05:09,887 --> 00:05:13,718
After both boards are up, say what A takes
home

126
00:05:13,738 --> 00:05:15,643
and what B takes home.

127
00:05:15,663 --> 00:05:20,265
One cell is one morning for two carts, not
a score for

128
00:05:20,285 --> 00:05:21,420
one of them.

129
00:05:21,440 --> 00:05:23,014
Here is the idea.

130
00:05:23,034 --> 00:05:25,803
The first number is always Cart A.

131
00:05:25,823 --> 00:05:28,194
The second is always Cart B.

132
00:05:28,214 --> 00:05:32,178
Use one busy hour in every cell, so the
four

133
00:05:32,198 --> 00:05:33,772
mornings can be compared.

134
00:05:33,792 --> 00:05:35,764
That pair is the payoff.

135
00:05:35,784 --> 00:05:39,350
It is what each cart takes home that hour.

136
00:05:39,370 --> 00:05:40,907
Look at the table.

137
00:05:40,927 --> 00:05:42,464
A is the row.

138
00:05:42,484 --> 00:05:44,020
B is the column.

139
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:46,745
High and Low sit on the edges.

140
00:05:46,765 --> 00:05:49,858
If both stay High, each takes home three.

141
00:05:49,878 --> 00:05:54,529
If A stays High and B cuts Low, customers
walk to B.

142
00:05:54,549 --> 00:05:58,810
A takes home zero that hour, and B takes
home five.

143
00:05:58,830 --> 00:06:02,656
Now both carts cut, because neither wants
to be the

144
00:06:02,676 --> 00:06:03,549
expensive board.

145
00:06:03,569 --> 00:06:05,087
Read one and one.

146
00:06:05,107 --> 00:06:06,626
Not five and five.

147
00:06:06,646 --> 00:06:10,472
Five only appears if the other cart is
still selling

148
00:06:10,492 --> 00:06:12,780
High, and that morning is gone.

149
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:14,771
Read a cell out loud.

150
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:16,762
Who is the first number?

151
00:06:16,782 --> 00:06:20,745
What does zero then five say happened on
the path?

152
00:06:20,765 --> 00:06:25,523
If you can do that for every cell, the
morning is on

153
00:06:25,543 --> 00:06:26,399
paper.

154
00:06:26,419 --> 00:06:28,391
Next we close the unit.

155
00:06:28,411 --> 00:06:30,780
Nobody has picked a cell yet.

156
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:32,844
Look back at the path.

157
00:06:32,864 --> 00:06:34,817
You can name the players.

158
00:06:34,837 --> 00:06:37,975
You can name the strategies, High or Low.

159
00:06:37,995 --> 00:06:41,133
You can read the payoffs in each cell.

160
00:06:41,153 --> 00:06:43,502
That is the game on paper.

161
00:06:43,522 --> 00:06:46,660
That is as far as this unit goes.

162
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:51,022
That is all I need you to take from this
unit.

163
00:06:51,042 --> 00:06:52,609
The table is written.

164
00:06:52,629 --> 00:06:54,591
Nobody has picked a cell.

165
00:06:54,611 --> 00:06:58,557
What each cart would pick from that table
is the

166
00:06:58,577 --> 00:06:59,450
next sitting.
